// The Piscatoris hunter area - mapsquares 36_55 and 36_56, and the west of 37_55 and 37_56 (the falconry
// enclosure) - from the rev 474 cache by tools/models/import474rect.py.
//
// 377 HAS THE GROUND ALREADY, and most of what stands on it: the same heights and overlays, 3,385 and
// 3,130 of the two squares' locs. What it lacks is the way in. Every tile of both squares is flagged
// blocked, as are the western halves of 37_55/37_56 - a landscape Jagex had built and closed off - and
// the Hunter things themselves are missing: the tracking plants, burrows and bushes, the deadfall
// boulders, rabbit holes, the falconer's perches and stile. So the rects bring 474's tile flags and its
// locs. Checked before and after: the terrain differs only in those flags, except
//   - 84 tiles along 36_55's south edge, where 474 re-coloured the underlay to meet its own new 36_54
//     (Eagles' Peak) - those keep 377's underlay, so the seam with 377's 36_54 does not change;
//   - 35 tiles in 36_56 given heights for a bank of rock - taken, as they are inside the square.
// A loc the 377 map already had keeps its 377 id and its line (the colony's rocks, the fairy ring - which
// 474 moved to a ground-decoration slot and stays in 377's), and 474's area-sound and minimap-icon locs
// (16403-16446, 19750, and 19583, a tracking-marker transformer with no default) are not placed.
//
// THE TRACKING NODES are kept as locs of their own. 474 gives every plant on a trail its own id; by
// looks alone the importer would have made them the 377 plants they are copies of (opless) and the
// burrows and bushes the Feldip ones (whose Inspect starts a Feldip weasel trail). So they come in as
// one type per look - four plants, one burrow and one bush per tracking ground - on the models of the
// objects they copy. The plants carry category=hunter_pisc_track_node, one trigger for all of them.
//
// Ops, so that none is a dead click:
//   - the plants' and burrows' Inspect and the bushes' Search/Attack: common kebbit (south, 36_55) and
//     razor-backed kebbit (north, 36_56) tracking - scripts/hunter_piscatoris.rs2;
//   - the stile's Climb-over: the falconry enclosure's only way in - scripts/hunter_falconry.rs2;
//   - the boulders (loc474_19205, Feldip's) already carry the deadfall's Set-trap;
//   - the rabbit hole's Flush is commented out: rabbits and ferreting were never finished (OSRS added
//     rabbit snaring in 2024), and nothing here handles it.

